*Heading
 Net pull-out, ALTERNATED weave -- JOB 4/5 of the restart chain: Phase D (FREE) -- quadratic C3D10M, alpha=1000 damping (beta=0)
** ==========================================================================
** Restart-continuation job: picks up the full model state at the end of
** job 3 (net_pullout_phaseC_release).
**
** Submit with:
**   abaqus job=net_pullout_phaseD_free oldjob=net_pullout_phaseC_release \
**          input=net_pullout_phaseD_free.inp interactive
**
** Release the central x-beam's LEFT clamp entirely (no longer position-
** constrained in any of the 3 translational dof). Removing a BC in
** Abaqus/Explicit requires *Boundary, op=NEW restating every OTHER
** currently-active BC (op=NEW wipes the full BC table for this step
** onward) while simply omitting the one being released. All restated
** values are UNCHANGED from their current state (held, not ramped) --
** this step's only physical change is the X_BEAM_2_END_NEG omission.
**
** This is the single most abrupt event in the whole chain (a genuine
** topology change, not a ramped value) and the shortest step (0.05 s),
** so intra-step restart checkpoints are the densest here relative to
** step length (every 0.0125 s, 4 across the step).
**
** *Restart, read, step=N uses the GLOBAL CUMULATIVE step number across
** the whole chain, not a number relative to oldjob=: restart files are
** cumulative, so step=1 always means "global step 1" (job A's ENGAGE)
** regardless of which oldjob= is used to get there. This job (D) is
** global step 4 (A=1, B=2, C=3, D=4), so it reads step=3 (C's own
** RELEASE step) to continue from C, not from A.
** ==========================================================================
*Restart, read, step=3
